IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vet-training`
IMPORT `vet-qa`

-- Vocational Education and Training Act 1996 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (vet-qa.l4): every exported question, for
-- every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for every role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes the situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value
-- that makes it not hold and every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the apprentice (the
-- baseline's seat) the answer is also asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. For the
-- employer and the provider the answers are worked by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts: the baseline's fixtures, copied (Jake's TAFE course, k024 and k030, with the baseline's HYPOTHETICAL labels;
-- Liam, the baseline's illustrative apprentice electrician, not one of the lives). Expected values are written by hand
-- from the deposited text, never copied from the output. The mechanical cases at the end are generated by the
-- scratchpad script gen_vet.py from the layer's own @export list.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked stand` IS A `Where the training contract stands`
ASSUME `an unasked provider` IS A `My provider`
ASSUME `an unasked class` IS A `Qualification class`
ASSUME `an unasked route` IS A Route
ASSUME `an unasked contract` IS A `The contract's terms`
ASSUME `an unasked place` IS A `Where I am training`
ASSUME `an unasked lodgement` IS A `My lodgement`
ASSUME `an unasked change` IS A Change
ASSUME `an unasked party` IS A Party
ASSUME `an unasked termination` IS A `My termination`
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A `My employer's reason`
ASSUME `an unasked status` IS A `What has happened to the contract`
ASSUME `an unasked completion` IS A `My completion`
ASSUME `an unasked decision` IS A Decision
ASSUME `an unasked outcome` IS AN `Appeal outcome`
ASSUME `an unasked outcome I want` IS A `What I want the Commission to do`
ASSUME `an unasked offence` IS AN Offence
ASSUME `an unasked reason of mine` IS A `The reason I give`
ASSUME `an unasked decision of mine` IS A `The decision I am dissatisfied with`
ASSUME `an unasked employer's offence` IS A `The employer's offence`
ASSUME `an unasked person's completion` IS A `The person's completion`

`as the apprentice` MEANS `I am an apprentice or trainee, or about to become one`
`as the employer` MEANS `I employ an apprentice or trainee, or am about to take one on`
`as the provider` MEANS `I run a training provider`

`no contract` MEANS `there is no training contract, and none is proposed`
`proposed` MEANS `a training contract is proposed or signed, but not registered yet`
`registered` MEANS `the training contract has been registered`

§§ `Fixtures (the baseline's, copied)`

-- HYPOTHETICAL: the TAFE college registered and permitted to deliver Jake's courses (s 58A).
`the TAFE college` MEANS `My provider` WITH
    `is a registered training provider` IS TRUE
    `is permitted by its registration conditions, the accreditation and the Council's orders` IS TRUE
    `acts for a registered training provider that monitors it` IS FALSE

`an unregistered provider` MEANS `My provider` WITH
    `is a registered training provider` IS FALSE
    `is permitted by its registration conditions, the accreditation and the Council's orders` IS FALSE
    `acts for a registered training provider that monitors it` IS FALSE

`a monitored partner of a registered provider` MEANS `My provider` WITH
    `is a registered training provider` IS FALSE
    `is permitted by its registration conditions, the accreditation and the Council's orders` IS FALSE
    `acts for a registered training provider that monitors it` IS TRUE

-- HYPOTHETICAL (Liam): a contract with every s 60E limb, for an electrical qualification taken as class A.
`Liam's electrical apprenticeship contract` MEANS `My contract` WITH
    `an employer agrees I will be employed while I fulfil it to obtain the qualification` IS TRUE
    `my employer agrees to train me under it` IS TRUE
    `my employer agrees to let me fulfil my obligations and be trained and assessed` IS TRUE
    `my employer agrees my training and assessment time is working time, including for pay` IS TRUE
    `I agree to fulfil my obligations and to be trained and assessed` IS TRUE
    `it states the qualification` IS TRUE
    `the class of that qualification` IS `class A`
    `it complies with the regulations` IS TRUE
    `the number of employers` IS 1
    `the chief executive approved more than one employer` IS FALSE

-- k024/k030: Jake's TAFE enrolment has no employer, so none of the employer's s 60E(1)(a) promises (Certificate II
-- taken as class C: HYPOTHETICAL).
