-- The baseline's fixtures, put as the layer asks them: the employer's four s 60E(1)(a) agreements as the one fact that
-- all four hold (the layer's QA-6), and a contract's status without whether it is registered, which the situation input
-- gives (QA-7). The cases that compare with the baseline pass the baseline the fixture itself.
GIVEN c IS A `My contract`
GIVETH A `The contract's terms`
`the terms of` c MEANS
    `The contract's terms` WITH
        `the employer agrees to employ the apprentice while they fulfil it, to train them, to let them be trained and assessed, and to count that time as working time, including for pay` IS
                c's `an employer agrees I will be employed while I fulfil it to obtain the qualification`
            AND c's `my employer agrees to train me under it`
            AND c's `my employer agrees to let me fulfil my obligations and be trained and assessed`
            AND c's `my employer agrees my training and assessment time is working time, including for pay`
        `the apprentice agrees to fulfil their obligations and to be trained and assessed` IS c's `I agree to fulfil my obligations and to be trained and assessed`
        `the contract states the qualification` IS c's `it states the qualification`
        `the class of the qualification it states` IS c's `the class of that qualification`
        `the contract complies with the regulations` IS c's `it complies with the regulations`
        `how many employers are parties to it` IS c's `the number of employers`
        `the chief executive approved there being more than one employer` IS c's `the chief executive approved more than one employer`

GIVEN st IS A `My contract's status`
GIVETH A `What has happened to the contract`
`what happened to` st MEANS
    `What has happened to the contract` WITH
        `the chief executive has cancelled its registration` IS st's `its registration has been cancelled`
        `the contract has been terminated` IS st's `it has been terminated`
        `the contract has expired` IS st's `it has expired`

-- The provider's view of a person (s 60D(1), s 60I): f, fulfilled a registered training contract; c, completed an
-- approved course; a, assessed competent; e, the skills come from training with an employer.
GIVEN f IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The person's completion`
`a person who` f c a e MEANS
    `The person's completion` WITH
        `they fulfilled their obligations under a registered training contract` IS f
        `they completed an approved VET course for it` IS c
        `I assessed them and am satisfied they have the skills and competency` IS a
        `their skills come from training with an employer and other learning` IS e

