-- ss 60(b), (c): at 18 alone; under 18 only if the regulations give capacity and require no parent's signature.
#ASSERT `Can I sign my training contract on my own, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` 17 TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I sign my training contract on my own, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` 17 TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can I sign my training contract on my own, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` 18 FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Can I sign my training contract on my own, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` 16 FALSE FALSE EQUALS no

-- s 60B: Part 7 prevails over an inconsistent award.
#ASSERT `Which prevails, Part 7 or my award, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` TRUE EQUALS `the answer is` `Part 7 and its regulations prevail over the award`
#ASSERT `Which prevails, Part 7 or my award, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` FALSE EQUALS `the answer is` `no conflict: both apply`

-- s 60F(1)-(3): not started until registered; the employer lodges; refusal open only on a ground.
#ASSERT `Has my training contract started, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Has my training contract started, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my contract be refused registration, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` `lodged in order` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May my contract be refused registration, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` `an employer the chief executive finds unfit` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Who must lodge my training contract, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `proposed` EQUALS `the answer is` `my employer`

-- s 60E(4), s 60F(4): a variation by both, a suspension by either, a transfer by the employer; only a variation lodged.
#ASSERT `Who may make this change, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` `a variation` EQUALS `the answer is` `my employer and I together`
#ASSERT `Who may make this change, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` `a suspension` EQUALS `the answer is` `either my employer or I, alone`
#ASSERT `Who may make this change, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` `a transfer to another employer` EQUALS `the answer is` `my employer alone, to another person who employs me`
#ASSERT `May my contract be transferred to this employer, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May my contract be transferred to this employer, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I suspend my training contract, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I suspend my training contract, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Must this change to my contract be lodged, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` `a variation` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Must this change to my contract be lodged, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` `a suspension` EQUALS no

-- s 60G: protected after probation, or from the start with none; the employer may end it then only with consent or
-- approval; the apprentice may end it (subject to the regulations); the chief executive must approve on the four grounds.
#ASSERT `Am I protected from termination without my consent, as I ask it` `as the apprentice` `registered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
